Source: new-lg4ff
Section: kernel
Priority: optional
Maintainer: marth <marthofdoom@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13)
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://github.com/marthofdoom/new-lg4ff
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: new-lg4ff-dkms
Architecture: all
Depends: dkms, ${misc:Depends}
Recommends: linux-headers-generic | linux-headers-amd64 | pve-headers
Provides: hid-logitech-new
Description: improved Logitech wheel force feedback driver (DKMS)
 Replacement for the in-kernel hid-logitech module for Logitech steering
 wheels (G29, G27, G25, G923 PS, Driving Force GT/Pro, MOMO, ...): all Linux
 force feedback effect types rendered at 500 Hz, software-rendered condition
 effects when the hardware slots are full, real friction and rumble on the
 G29, steering sensitivity curve, persistent centering spring, gain up to
 150 %, and sysfs controls for everything (used by Oversteer).
 .
 The module is built for each installed kernel through DKMS and replaces
 hid-logitech.
